98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 80 0 R
/E (Modern cities face an escalating crisis driven by rapid urbanisation and population growth. Traffic congestion costs economies billions annually in lost productivity, while inefficient waste collection and disposal systems contribute to environmental degradation and public health risks. Air and noise pollution from vehicle emissions and industrial activity continue to worsen, disproportionately affecting vulnerable communities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 80 0 R
/E (Energy consumption in urban environments is poorly optimised, with buildings, street lighting, and transportation networks operating without intelligent coordination. Water and resource management systems remain largely reactive rather than predictive, leading to significant waste and infrastructure strain.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
