103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Smart Cities leverage interconnected digital infrastructure to enhance urban living. Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) enables real-time decision-making by analysing vast datasets from city systems, optimising traffic flow, energy distribution, and public services. Machine learning algorithms continuously improve predictions, reducing operational costs and improving citizen outcomes across transportation, utilities, and emergency response.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The Internet of Things \(IoT\) forms the sensory backbone of smart urban environments, with millions of embedded devices collecting live data on air quality, energy consumption, waste levels, and mobility patterns. Data analytics platforms process these streams to surface actionable insights for city planners and administrators. Together, AI, IoT, and data analytics create an adaptive, self-optimising urban ecosystem capable of addressing congestion, pollution, and resource inefficiency at scale.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
